g", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}]}], "type": "scholar", "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Unified Modelling Language, UML 2.0: Differences with Basic UML ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about UML.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Assess the incident of data in the macrosystem processes, based on the data dictionary to consolidate intervening data, based in established parameters.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.  Exchanges simple information on programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe8n2le02ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Simple Past statements with be and other verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>When you want to talk about things that happened and already ended use the <strong>simple past</strong>.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I thought they were identical.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In 1997 they created UML as a standard language to construct, visualize and document the artifacts of software systems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To use the simple past you need the past form of the verb.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Follow this structure to form <strong>affirmative</strong><strong>statements</strong> in <strong>past</strong>:&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject + <strong>verb in past</strong> + complement.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To make <strong>negative</strong><strong>sentences</strong> in <strong>past</strong> you need to see if the verb is <i>be</i> or other verb.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If the verb is <i>be</i>, follow this structure:&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject + <strong>was or were </strong>+ <strong>not</strong> + complement.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For other verbs, use this structure:&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject + <strong>did</strong> + <strong>not</strong> + <strong>main verb in</strong><strong>infinitive</strong> + complement.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Example:</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><i>UML 2.0 <strong>added </strong>new features to make things easier.&nbsp;<br /> UML <strong>was</strong> really basic</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Some common regular and irregular verbs with their past form are in the chart below:</p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"><strong>Verb in present</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\"><strong>Verb in past</strong></p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Was/ Were\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Say \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Said\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Go\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Went\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Come\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Came\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Add\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Added\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Call\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Called\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Create\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Created\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"launch\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"launched\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I suppose that they created the new structure to answer a goal of restructuring and polishing UML.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "identical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "exactly the same in appearance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I thought they were identical.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe8n2le02ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "visualize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to form a mental image", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In 1997 they created UML as a standard language to construct, visualize and document the artifacts of software systems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe8n2le02ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "advantage", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a feature that is good and helps you succeed ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: With UML 2.0 we have the advantage of adding new features that we can use in an extensive way to develop models and their corresponding systems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe8n2le02ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "extensive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "of wide extent", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: With UML 2.0 we have the advantage of adding new features that we can use in an extensive way to develop models and their corresponding systems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe8n2le02ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "infrastructure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the basic framework of a system", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Firstly, its infrastructure; it defines the basic constructs of the language and you use it to give mechanisms of adjustment, providing a reusable meta- language core.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe8n2le02ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Search for more new features in UML 2.0.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a description of such features.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your writing with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I can list the improvements of UML 2.0.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can interpret and explain the improvements of UML 2.0.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can discuss about UML.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Verbs with Infinitives, need to, in questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When you want to talk about actions that are necessities in the contexts you are talking, use <strong>need to</strong>.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When someone ask if something is necessary they use <strong>need to</strong>.&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Follow this structure to ask in present using <strong>need to</strong>:&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Auxiliary (Do/ Does) + subject+ <strong>need to</strong>+ <strong>verb in infinitive</strong>+ complement + ?&nbsp;<br /></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Examples:</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><i>Does she <strong>need to use</strong> a heading in her page?&nbsp;<br /> Do you <strong>need to create</strong> a web page?</i></p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<table style=\"border-color: black;\"> <tbody> <tr> <td width=\"81\"> <p><strong>Auxiliary </strong></p> </td> <td width=\"85\"> <p><strong>Subject</strong></p> </td> <td width=\"132\"> <p><strong>Need to</strong></p> </td> <td width=\"149\"> <p><strong>verb</strong></p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td width=\"81\"> <p>Do</p> </td> <td width=\"85\"> <p>we</p> </td> <td width=\"132\"> <p>need to</p> </td> <td width=\"149\"> <p>create?</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td width=\"81\"> <p>Does</p> </td> <td width=\"85\"> <p>he</p> </td> <td width=\"132\"> <p>need to</p> </td> <td width=\"149\"> <p>write?</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td width=\"81\"> <p>Do</p> </td> <td width=\"85\"> <p>I</p> </td> <td width=\"132\"> <p>need to</p> </td> <td width=\"149\"> <p>use a programming language?</p> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do we need to use UML or UML 2.0 for this task?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do we need to understand UML as a programming language?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do we have a way to differentiate UML from UML 2.0?", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "superstructure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the overlying framework of a system", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Secondly, its superstructure; it defines the users' constructs and you use to provide better support and better options for the software modeling and behavior, improving the constructs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe8n2le02ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}]}